  "id": "low-light",
  "name": "Low Light",
  "tagline": "Night air, distant glass, a pulse that comes and goes.",
  "description": "Night air in gusts and a slow, breathing pad. Glass tones ring far off in the room, about one every half minute. A half-time heartbeat that comes and goes; dub chords far back.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Incubate",
    "for": "Stepping back from a problem after a focus block.",
    "why": "Low demand but mildly engaging, as the plan's Incubate state asks. The pulse is soft and half-time and is not always there; the pad comes forward; glass tones arrive slowly from far off, enough to hold you lightly while the problem works in the background. The evidence that incubation helps is weak and contested, so treat this as an experiment."
  },
